        "v": 5,
        "title": "gravity-ad request body omits surface field when null",
        "summary": "use-gravity-ad.ts conditionally spreads the surface field into the JSON request body, omitting it entirely when null or undefined. Previously, the field defaulted to 'chat' in the payload. This change prevents sending an explicit surface value when one is not provided by the caller.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T15:50:23.622Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the assistant asks for a targeted ad, it used to always say the request came from 'chat' even when no specific place was given. Now it simply leaves that label out of the message entirely instead of sending a default value. You wouldn't notice this directly unless you were inspecting the network traffic between the app and the ad server, where the request body will now show one fewer field when no surface is provided.",
