        "title": "DynamicAgentTemplateSchema accepts spawnagentinline and handleSteps",
        "summary": "DynamicAgentTemplateSchema refine rule now permits 'spawn_agent_inline' tool or programmatic 'handleSteps' generator when spawnableAgents is non-empty. Previously required only 'spawn_agents' tool in toolNames. Covers common/src/types/dynamic-agent-template.ts. Error message updated to mention handleSteps alternative for spawnableAgents validation.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T15:50:29.735Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You're building an AI assistant that can spawn helper sub-agents. The system now lets you launch those helpers inline (during a turn) instead of only at setup time, using new inline or programmatic spawn paths. If you tried to configure a template with spawnableAgents but no 'spawn_agents' tool, it previously failed validation; it now accepts 'spawn_agent_inline' or a handleSteps generator as valid alternatives. This is live today for templates that define spawnable agents, and the clearer error message tells you exactly which spawning option to add.",
