        "v": 11,
        "title": "SDK terminal command detaches on all platforms",
        "summary": "The `spawn` call in `runTerminalCommand` now sets detached: true unconditionally, replacing the previous `detached: !isWindows`. The updated comment states that on POSIX a negative pid kills the process group and that on Windows detached: true maps to `DETACHED_PROCESS`, which with `windowsHide` fully detaches the child from the parent's console.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `sdk/src/tools/run-terminal-command.ts`, the `spawn` options block changes `detached: !isWindows` to detached: true and rewrites the adjacent comment to describe a process group on POSIX using a negative pid kill and detached: true mapping to `DETACHED_PROCESS` on Windows. The `killProcessGroup` helper and `liveChildren`/`installExitSweep` exit sweep logic are unchanged in the hunk.",
