        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix terminal focus detection via CSI regex",
        "summary": "Replaced naive substring checks with regex `FOCUS_EVENT_RE` to match complete CSI focus sequences (`ESC [ I` and `ESC [ O`). This prevents unrelated bytes in batched stdin chunks from triggering false focus events. Added `parseFocusState` to determine net focus state from the last event in a chunk and track `lastReported` state to avoid re-renders from repeated identical events. Covers `cli/src/hooks/use-terminal-focus.ts`.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T15:48:40.418Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you switch away from or back to the CLI's terminal window, other keystrokes or pasted text sometimes got mistaken for focus changes, causing the screen to flicker or go dim at the wrong time. The program now looks for the exact focus codes (ESC [ I for focus gained, ESC [ O for focus lost) and only acts on them, ignoring unrelated bytes that happen to share the same chunk. It also remembers the last focus state it acted on, so a terminal that repeats the same focus message won't trigger repeated screen updates. This fix is live today in the CLI for anyone running it on a terminal that supports focus reporting.",
